+# rather than leave the reader to find out: the SIDECAR verifies (it names one
+# file, and that file was just built). The cumulative manifest does NOT verify
+# as a whole — it keeps lines for tarballs of OTHER versions, `npm/*.tgz` is
+# git-ignored so a fresh clone has none of them on disk, and a bulk check
