.claude/scripts/tests/fixtures/sample_audit_log.jsonl:50:{"ts":"2026-04-11T21:38:56Z","action":"agent_spawn","session_id":"s-d","project":"/repo","tool":"Agent","subagent_type":"general-purpose","desc_preview":"Final smoke test of the framework","desc_hash":"aa00000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000050","skill":"ceo-orchestration","has_profile":true,"has_file_assignment":true,"prompt_len_bucket":"<4096","response_kind":"text","hook_duration_ms":16}
     1	#!/usr/bin/env python3
     2	"""PostToolUse Agent audit log — Python single-file hook with rotation.
     3	
     4	Port of `.claude/scripts/audit-log.sh` to stdlib Python. Bash version
     5	remains untouched until A.4 flips settings.json to the Python shim.
     6	
     7	## Schema
     8	
     9	Identical to AUDIT-LOG-SCHEMA.md with these additions:
    10	
    11	- `hook_duration_ms` (integer) — wallclock duration of the hook itself,
    12	  measured at end of processing. Enables `audit-query.py stats --latency`
    13	  analysis in Sprint 3 without re-instrumenting the hooks.
    14	
    15	PLAN-020 Phase 0 item 1 (audit-log v2.7 schema bump — ADDITIVE):
    16	
    17	- `usage_metadata` (object|null) — Anthropic API usage_metadata
    18	  passthrough. Keys: `cache_creation_input_tokens`,
    19	  `cache_read_input_tokens`, `uncached_input_tokens`, `output_tokens`,
    20	  `thinking_tokens`. Each is integer or null. Captured per spawn for
    21	  cache-coverage analysis (PLAN-020 §6 sub-target measurement).
    22	- `cache_coverage_bps` (int|null) — derived metric in integer
    23	  basis-points (ratio × 10000, clamped [0, 10000]):
    24	  `cache_read / (cache_read + cache_creation + uncached)`. Null if
    25	  totals unavailable. PLAN-020 §6 acceptance: P50 +10pp vs Phase 0
    26	  baseline. PLAN-118 WS-E (S181): replaced the legacy `cache_coverage`
    27	  float — floats break the HMAC-covered payload (canonical_json
    28	  no-float invariant). The derivation helper still returns the float
    29	  ratio; the producer converts to bps before the entry dict.
    30	- `rail` (string|null) — spawn dispatch rail: `"native"` |
    31	  `"custom"` | null (legacy / unknown). Discriminator for ADR-050
    32	  dual-rail A/B harness. PLAN-019 emitters (pre-PLAN-020) emit null;
    33	  PLAN-020 Phase 1+ emitters set the value.
    34	
    35	All three fields are ADDITIVE — older consumers ignore them safely.
    36	
    37	PLAN-021 ADR-052 (audit-log v2.8 schema bump — ADDITIVE):
    38	
    39	- `model` (string|null) — Claude model ID used for the spawn. Values
    40	  are canonical Anthropic IDs: `"claude-opus-4-8"`,
    41	  `"claude-sonnet-4-6"`, `"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001"`, or null if
    42	  unknown. Captured from `tool_response.model` when Anthropic API
    43	  emits it, else null. Enables forensic correlation: if a
    44	  Sonnet-routed review misses a bug, the audit log proves which
    45	  model made the decision.
    46	
    47	Field is ADDITIVE — older consumers ignore; pre-v2.8 emitters emit
    48	null.
    49	
    50	PLAN-065 Phase 1 (audit-log v2.15 — extract_skill 3-path matrix):
    51	
    52	- `extract_skill()` ports the validated 3-path logic from
    53	  `.claude/scripts/extract-skill.py` (58 tests, ReDoS-hardened) inline
    54	  into the hook so audit-log emit covers Format-A inline / Format-B
    55	  reference / Format-C `## SKILL CONTENT` block fallback. Restores
    56	  observability of `skill=<name>` post-ADR-082 mitigated dispatch +
    57	  Format-B SKILL REFERENCE default flip. Pre-Phase 1 baseline: 24/24
    58	  agent_spawn rows had `skill="unknown"` (100% loss). Target ≤10%
    59	  unknown in 30d post-merge.
    60	
    61	  Sec MF-7 hardening: NFKC normalize, NUL byte denied, length cap
    62	  256 chars on captured group, path traversal denied (the captured
    63	  group grammar excludes `/` `..` `\\`), regex bounded quantifiers
    64	  `{0,255}` (no nested unbounded alternation — ReDoS-safe).
    65	
    66	PLAN-079 (extract_skill Path D — canonical archetype mapping):
    67	
    68	- Path D added to `extract_skill()` as a TAIL fallback (after Paths
    69	  A/B/C miss). Maps the 5 canonical archetypes — `code-reviewer`,
    70	  `security-engineer`, `qa-architect`, `performance-engineer`,
    71	  `devops` — to their canonical skill names per ADR-051 (sub-agents
    72	  load skills via `.claude/agents/<name>.md` reference, not inline).
    73	  Closes the observability gap S87/S88 surfaced (20/26 unknown
    74	  agent_spawn rows on canonical-archetype dispatches without
    75	  inline SKILL CONTENT).
    76	
    77	  Backwards compat: signature changed from `extract_skill(prompt)`
    78	  to `extract_skill(prompt, subagent_type="")` — default arg
    79	  preserves all single-arg callers. Frozen mapping constant
    80	  `_ARCHETYPE_TO_SKILL` (no runtime I/O); drift-detector test
    81	  (`test_audit_log_path_d.py`) asserts the table matches the
    82	  "Loads <skill> skill via reference" phrase in each
    83	  `.claude/agents/<archetype>.md` description frontmatter.
    84	
    85	  Sec MF-7 defense-in-depth: `subagent_type` is normalized via
    86	  `strip().lower()` (case-fold mirrors `check_agent_spawn.py:204`
    87	  archetype-routing precedent), then validated POST-NORMALIZE
    88	  against `_ARCHETYPE_NAME_RE` (`^[a-z][a-z0-9\\-]{0,63}$` with
    89	  `.fullmatch`). A raw-length pre-bound (`len > 80`) caps
    90	  hot-path allocation. Rejected silently: slash, dot-traversal,
    91	  NUL, unicode, oversize, non-string. Uppercase is INTENTIONALLY
    92	  case-folded (NOT rejected) — matches Agent-tool emitter
    93	  flexibility for the routing layer.
    94	
    95	## Rotation
    96	
    97	NEW in Sprint 2: monthly rotation by size threshold.
    98	
    99	Before writing, if `audit-log.jsonl` exists and its size > ROTATE_AT_BYTES
   100	(default 10 MB), rename to `audit-log-YYYY-MM.jsonl` (current month) and
   101	start a fresh file. If the monthly file already exists (second rotation
   102	in the same month), append `-1`, `-2`, etc.
   103	
   104	The rotation rename happens UNDER the lock so a concurrent writer can't
   105	append to a file that's about to be moved.
   106	
   107	## Safety properties
   108	
   109	1. Fail-open: any exception writes a breadcrumb to `audit-log.errors`
   110	   and exits 0. The user's session MUST NOT be blocked by this hook.
   111	2. Silent on stdout: composable with the reminder hook.
   112	3. Env-var overrides (`CEO_AUDIT_LOG_*`) for testability.
   113	4. Redaction via `_lib.redact` (property-tested).
   114	5. Locking via `_lib.filelock` (fcntl.flock).
   115	
   116	## Decomposition candidates
   117	
   118	This module has accreted ~7 responsibilities across PLAN-019..PLAN-079.
   119	Tracked decomposition targets for PLAN-085+ readers (NO extraction in
   120	PLAN-087 — doc-only surface; per `F-A-CR-D0016` P2 + PLAN-084 evolution
   121	roadmap):
   122	
   123	- **Path A — `extract_skill()` extraction.** Lines for the 3-path
   124	  matrix (Format-A inline / Format-B reference / Format-C ``## SKILL
   125	  CONTENT`` block) plus Path D canonical archetype map are a
   126	  self-contained extraction target. Candidate destination:
   127	  `_lib/skill_extract.py` (already exists as the standalone module
   128	  `.claude/scripts/extract-skill.py` — the in-hook copy duplicates
   129	  logic kept inline so audit-log emit covers the dispatch hot path
   130	  without subprocess fork). Extraction would centralize the regex
   131	  contract; trade-off is per-spawn import cost.
   132	- **Path B — `usage_metadata` / `cache_coverage_bps` derivation.** The
   133	  v2.7 / v2.8 schema bump logic (lines ~15-43 in this docstring) is
   134	  arithmetic on `tool_response`. Candidate destination:
   135	  `_lib/usage_metadata.py` (mirrors `_lib/tokens.py` adapter pattern).
   136	- **Path C — HMAC chain integration.** The audit-chain HMAC writer
   137	  is currently invoked from this hook's main path. Candidate
   138	  destination: `_lib/audit_hmac.py` (already exists as the HMAC
   139	  verifier — the writer-side wrapper would mirror the
   140	  ``verify_chain()`` API). Extraction unblocks the two-writer
   141	  asymmetry surfaced as PLAN-084 finding C.1.
   142	- **Path D — Orchestrator split.** The PostToolUse dispatch logic
   143	  (rotation + redaction + emit + HMAC + breadcrumb fallback) is the
   144	  remaining "orchestrator" after Paths A/B/C peel off. Candidate
   145	  destination: keep `audit_log.py` as a ~150-line thin shim that
   146	  delegates to the four `_lib/*` modules.
   147	
   148	Each Path is sized to one PLAN-08x phase; extraction order is
   149	A → C → B → D (Path C unblocks the two-writer fix, so it lands
   150	ahead of B/D).
   151	"""
   152	
   153	from __future__ import annotations
   154	
   155	import getpass
   156	import json
   157	import os
   158	import re
   159	import stat
   160	import sys
   161	import time
   162	import unicodedata
   163	from datetime import datetime, timezone
   164	from pathlib import Path
   165	from typing import Any, Dict, Optional, Tuple
   166	
   167	# Make `.claude/hooks/` importable so `_lib` resolves.
   168	_HOOKS_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
   169	if str(_HOOKS_DIR) not in sys.path:
   170	    sys.path.insert(0, str(_HOOKS_DIR))
   171	
   172	from _lib import contract as _contract  # noqa: E402
   173	from _lib import payload as _payload  # noqa: E402  (response_kind helper)
   174	from _lib import redact as _redact  # noqa: E402
   175	from _lib import tokens as _tokens  # noqa: E402  (PLAN-006 Phase 5b / ADR-016)
   176	from _lib.adapters import claude as _claude_adapter  # noqa: E402
   177	from _lib.filelock import FileLock, FileLockTimeout  # noqa: E402
   178	
   179	
   180	# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   181	# Constants
   182	# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   183	
   184	# Default rotation threshold: 10 MB. Overridable via CEO_AUDIT_LOG_ROTATE_BYTES.
   185	DEFAULT_ROTATE_AT_BYTES = 10 * 1024 * 1024
   186	
   187	# PLAN-065 Phase 1 — Sec MF-7 input bounds.
   188	# Cap inputs at 1 MiB to keep the regex engine in linear-time territory.
   189	# Plans / prompts beyond this size are extreme outliers; rejecting them is
   190	# preferred over feeding pathological input to the regex engine.
   191	_MAX_INPUT_CHARS = 1024 * 1024  # 1 MiB hard cap
   192	_MAX_INPUT_BYTES = _MAX_INPUT_CHARS
   193	
   194	# Skill-name max length (PLAN-065 §4.1 fixture spec — 256-char cap).
   195	_MAX_SKILL_NAME_CHARS = 256
   196	
   197	# Allowed skill-name character class — ``[a-z0-9][a-z0-9\-]*`` anchored.
   198	# Used as defense-in-depth re-validation post-extract.
   199	_SKILL_NAME_CHARSET_RE = re.compile(r"^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9\-]*$")
   200	
   201	# PLAN-065 Phase 1 — 3-path SKILL extraction matrix.
   202	#
   203	# Path A — Format-A inline. Line-anchored ``^SKILL: <name>$``. Bounded
   204	# {0,255} quantifier on the captured group, no nested unbounded alternation
   205	# (ReDoS-safe). Mirrors the validated grammar in extract-skill.py:_PATH_A_RE.
   206	_SKILL_PATH_A_RE = re.compile(
   207	    r"(?m)^SKILL:[ \t]+([a-z0-9][a-z0-9\-]{0,255})\s*$",
   208	)
   209	
   210	# Path B — Format-B reference (mitigated dispatch + SKILL REFERENCE default).
   211	#   @.claude/skills/core/<name>/SKILL.md sha256=<64-hex>
   212	#   @.claude/skills/frontend/<name>/SKILL.md sha256=<64-hex>
   213	#   @.claude/skills/domains/<domain>/skills/<name>/SKILL.md sha256=<64-hex>
   214	# Captured group is the skill <name> path-segment, not the domain.
   215	_SKILL_PATH_B_RE = re.compile(
   216	    r"(?m)^@\.claude/skills/"
   217	    r"(?:core|frontend|domains/[a-z0-9][a-z0-9\-]{0,63}/skills)"
   218	    r"/([a-z0-9][a-z0-9\-]{0,255})/SKILL\.md"
   219	    r"\s+sha256=[0-9a-f]{64}\s*$",
   220	)
   221	
   222	# Path C — `## SKILL CONTENT` block fallback. Used when neither Format-A
   223	# nor Format-B was emitted (legacy / third-party adapter surface). The block
   224	# heading has a sibling `SKILL LOADED: <name>` annotation.
   225	_SKILL_PATH_C_HEADER_RE = re.compile(
   226	    r"(?m)^##[ \t]+SKILL[ \t]+CONTENT\b",
   227	)
   228	_SKILL_PATH_C_LOADED_RE = re.compile(
   229	    r"(?m)^SKILL[ \t]+LOADED:[ \t]+([a-z0-9][a-z0-9\-]{0,255})\s*$",
   230	)
   231	
   232	# PLAN-079 Path D — canonical archetype subagent_type → skill mapping.
   233	#
   234	# Sub-agent dispatches via ``Agent({subagent_type:"<archetype>"})`` load
   235	# their persona + skill via ``.claude/agents/<archetype>.md`` reference
   236	# per ADR-051 (PLAN-020). When the spawn prompt does NOT carry an
   237	# explicit Format-A/B/C SKILL envelope, Paths A-C all miss and the
   238	# pre-PLAN-079 behavior recorded ``skill="unknown"``. This frozen map
   239	# closes the observability gap by mapping the 5 canonical archetypes
   240	# to their loaded skill name. Frozen baseline pattern (mirrors
   241	# ``_FROZEN_BASELINE`` in tier_policy/_constants.py) — no runtime I/O
   242	# against agent files; drift-detector test asserts the table matches
   243	# the "Loads <skill> skill via reference" phrase in each
   244	# ``.claude/agents/<archetype>.md`` description frontmatter.
   245	_ARCHETYPE_TO_SKILL: Dict[str, str] = {
   246	    "code-reviewer": "code-review-checklist",
   247	    "security-engineer": "security-and-auth",
   248	    "qa-architect": "testing-strategy",
   249	    "performance-engineer": "performance-engineering",
   250	    "devops": "devops-ci-cd",
   251	    # PLAN-106 Wave B.2 (H3 fix) — additional archetypes recorded as
   252	    # `unknown` in 24h rolling because Path D lookup missed them. The
   253	    # canonical skill name on the right-hand side must match a real
   254	    # `.claude/skills/**/<name>/SKILL.md`. If the file is absent at
   255	    # adopter time the map still resolves the string; the downstream
   256	    # consumer is `audit_log.py:extract_skill()` Path D tail which
   257	    # records the string verbatim — no I/O.
   258	    "identity-trust-architect": "identity-and-trust-architecture",
   259	    "incident-commander": "incident-management",
   260	    "llm-finops-architect": "llm-routing-and-finops",
   500	    return False
   501	
   502	
   503	def _is_ghost_spawn_event(ev: Dict[str, Any]) -> bool:
   504	    """True iff the agent_spawn event is a harness ghost-event (no real payload).
   505	
   506	    All four conditions must hold simultaneously to avoid false-positives on
   507	    legitimate near-empty dispatches: empty desc, no rail attribution, no
   508	    profile marker, and SHA-of-empty-string desc_hash.
   509	    """
   510	    return (
   511	        ev.get("desc_preview") == ""
   512	        and ev.get("rail") is None
   513	        and ev.get("has_profile") is False
   514	        and ev.get("desc_hash") == _EMPTY_SHA256
   515	    )
   516	
   517	
   518	# PLAN-177 t2 (re-pass rc.4 P1-f). The POSITIVE half of the probe test.
   519	#
   520	# The S303 filter below identified a probe by ABSENCE alone — five governed
   521	# markers missing — and absence is the shape of the events the ratio exists to
   522	# find: a markerless real spawn (including one the PreToolUse hook admitted by
   523	# failing open) was classified as harness noise and removed from the
   524	# denominator. A probe-only window then reported green with
   525	# `harness_probes_skipped=1` while the governance gap it was built to surface
   526	# went unrendered.
   527	#
   528	# So the structural conditions are necessary, not sufficient: the row must ALSO
   529	# carry the observed harness signature. The signature is CLOSED — the literal
   530	# description the tool-materialization probe emits, anchored at both ends
   531	# (`Load <Tool> via ToolSearch?`, S303 observation, prompt `noop`) — plus
   532	# corroboration by `desc_hash`, which the emitter computes over the RAW
   533	# description: if the two disagree the preview was truncated or redacted, i.e.
   534	# not this short, secret-free probe line. Anything else counts. Every
   535	# uncertainty resolves toward VISIBLE.
   536	_HARNESS_PROBE_DESC_RE = re.compile(
   537	    r"\ALoad [A-Za-z0-9_.\-]+(?:,[ ]?[A-Za-z0-9_.\-]+)* via ToolSearch\?\Z"
   538	)
   539	
   540	
   541	def _has_harness_probe_fingerprint(ev: Dict[str, Any]) -> bool:
   542	    """True iff the row carries the CLOSED, observed harness-probe signature.
   543	
   544	    Positive identification, never inferred from missing fields. An absent or
   545	    non-matching `desc_hash` is NOT corroboration, so it returns False and the
   546	    row is counted — the safe direction for an advisory that exists to expose
   547	    unclassified spawns.
   548	    """
   549	    desc = ev.get("desc_preview")
   550	    if not isinstance(desc, str) or not _HARNESS_PROBE_DESC_RE.match(desc):
   551	        return False
   552	    digest = ev.get("desc_hash")
   553	    if not isinstance(digest, str) or not digest:
   554	        return False
   555	    return digest == hashlib.sha256(desc.encode("utf-8")).hexdigest()
